    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.visits\r\n\r\n### Question\r\n\r\nHi, I've been trying out `MiniVisits` and I really love it — great work!\r\n\r\nHowever, I'm a bit confused. I tried using `MiniVisits.add_path()`, but for some reason, the data doesn't persist after I exit Neovim. I'm not sure if that's the intended behavior, but I'd really like for it to save the visit automatically.\r\n\r\nHere's a short video demonstrating the issue:  \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b1d698d2-7835-413a-8f64-757e65bd6635\r\n\r\n\r\n<details><summary>Reproduction code:</summary>\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\r\nlocal mini_path = vim.fn.stdpath(\"data\") .. \"/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim\"\r\nlocal clone_cmd = { \"git\", \"clone\", \"--depth=1\", \"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim\", mini_path }\r\nvim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\r\nvim.cmd('echo \"`mini.nvim` is installed\" | redraw')\r\n\r\n-- Make sure 'mini.nvim' is available\r\nvim.cmd(\"packadd mini.nvim\")\r\nrequire(\"mini.deps\").setup()\r\nvim.cmd.colorscheme(\"randomhue\")\r\nrequire(\"mini.pick\").setup({})\r\nrequire(\"mini.extra\").setup({})\r\nrequire(\"mini.visits\").setup({\r\n\ttrack = {\r\n\t\tevent = \"\",\r\n\t},\r\n})\r\n```\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nI also tested `register_visit()`, and that *does* persist the visit, so I guess that's the proper way. Still, I'm wondering: why doesn't `add_path()` work the same way? Am I missing something?\r\n\r\nAny clarification or solution would be greatly appreciated. Thanks a lot!\r\n\r\n",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.visits</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hi, I've been trying out <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniVisits</code> and I really love it — great work!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">However, I'm a bit confused. I tried using <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniVisits.add_path()</code>, but for some reason, the data doesn't persist after I exit Neovim. I'm not sure if that's the intended behavior, but I'd really like for it to save the visit automatically.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Here's a short video demonstrating the issue:</p>\n<details open=\"\" class=\"details-reset border rounded-2\">\n  <summary class=\"tmp-px-3 py-2\">\n    <svg aria-hidden=\"true\" data-component=\"Octicon\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" data-view-component=\"true\" class=\"octicon octicon-device-camera-video\">\n    <path d=\"M16 3.75v8.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.136.643L11 10.575v.675A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 9.25 13h-7.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 0 11.25v-6.5C0 3.784.784 3 1.75 3h7.5c.966 0 1.75.784 1.75 1.75v.675l3.864-2.318A.75.75 0 0 1 16 3.75Zm-6.5 1a.25.25 0 0 0-.25-.25h-7.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25.25v6.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h7.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v-6.5ZM11 8.825l3.5 2.1v-5.85l-3.5 2.1Z\"></path>\n</svg>\n    <span class=\"m-1\">output_confuso.mp4</span>\n    <span class=\"dropdown-caret\"></span>\n  </summary>\n\n  <video src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/62192487/438617038-b1d698d2-7835-413a-8f64-757e65bd6635.mp4?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..Rdt3ERUkCwagaE28rhhHzUk6tqHQhQIkjxuDjZmY4t8\" data-canonical-src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/62192487/438617038-b1d698d2-7835-413a-8f64-757e65bd6635.mp4?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..Rdt3ERUkCwagaE28rhhHzUk6tqHQhQIkjxuDjZmY4t8\" controls=\"controls\" muted=\"muted\" class=\"d-block rounded-bottom-2 border-top width-fit\" style=\"max-height:640px; min-height: 200px\">\n\n  </video>\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Reproduction code:</summary>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.cmd('echo &quot;Installing `mini.nvim`&quot; | redraw')\nlocal mini_path = vim.fn.stdpath(&quot;data&quot;) .. &quot;/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim&quot;\nlocal clone_cmd = { &quot;git&quot;, &quot;clone&quot;, &quot;--depth=1&quot;, &quot;https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim&quot;, mini_path }\nvim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\nvim.cmd('echo &quot;`mini.nvim` is installed&quot; | redraw')\n\n-- Make sure 'mini.nvim' is available\nvim.cmd(&quot;packadd mini.nvim&quot;)\nrequire(&quot;mini.deps&quot;).setup()\nvim.cmd.colorscheme(&quot;randomhue&quot;)\nrequire(&quot;mini.pick&quot;).setup({})\nrequire(&quot;mini.extra&quot;).setup({})\nrequire(&quot;mini.visits&quot;).setup({\n\ttrack = {\n\t\tevent = &quot;&quot;,\n\t},\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">cmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)\n<span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">mini_path</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">fn</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">stdpath</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>data<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">..</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">clone_cmd</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>git<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>clone<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>--depth=1<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">mini_path</span> }\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">fn</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">system</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">clone_cmd</span>)\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">cmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>echo \"`mini.nvim` is installed\" | redraw<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)\n\n<span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Make sure 'mini.nvim' is available</span>\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">cmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>packadd mini.nvim<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>)\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>mini.deps<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>()\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">cmd</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">colorscheme</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>randomhue<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>)\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>mini.pick<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({})\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>mini.extra<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({})\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>mini.visits<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n\t<span class=\"pl-smi\">track</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n\t\t<span class=\"pl-smi\">event</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>,\n\t},\n})</pre></div>\n</details>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I also tested <code class=\"notranslate\">register_visit()</code>, and that <em>does</em> persist the visit, so I guess that's the proper way. Still, I'm wondering: why doesn't <code class=\"notranslate\">add_path()</code> work the same way? Am I missing something?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Any clarification or solution would be greatly appreciated. Thanks a lot!</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.visits\nQuestion\nHi, I've been trying out MiniVisits and I really love it — great work!\nHowever, I'm a bit confused. I tried using MiniVisits.add_path(), but for some reason, the data doesn't persist after I exit Neovim. I'm not sure if that's the intended behavior, but I'd really like for it to save the visit automatically.\nHere's a short video demonstrating the issue:\n\n  \n    \n    \n\n    output_confuso.mp4\n    \n  \n\n  \n\n  \n\n\nReproduction code:\nvim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\nlocal mini_path = vim.fn.stdpath(\"data\") .. \"/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim\"\nlocal clone_cmd = { \"git\", \"clone\", \"--depth=1\", \"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim\", mini_path }\nvim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\nvim.cmd('echo \"`mini.nvim` is installed\" | redraw')\n\n-- Make sure 'mini.nvim' is available\nvim.cmd(\"packadd mini.nvim\")\nrequire(\"mini.deps\").setup()\nvim.cmd.colorscheme(\"randomhue\")\nrequire(\"mini.pick\").setup({})\nrequire(\"mini.extra\").setup({})\nrequire(\"mini.visits\").setup({\n\ttrack = {\n\t\tevent = \"\",\n\t},\n})\n\nI also tested register_visit(), and that does persist the visit, so I guess that's the proper way. Still, I'm wondering: why doesn't add_path() work the same way? Am I missing something?\nAny clarification or solution would be greatly appreciated. Thanks a lot!",
