            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "`add_path()` is a helper that [ensures that path is present in the current index](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/doc/mini-visits.txt#L482-L484). If it wasn't there, its `count` and `latest` are 0, which means that entry will [get pruned during normalization](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/doc/mini-visits.txt#L910-L915) before writing to the disk (because `count` 0 is less than default [0.5 threshold](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/doc/mini-visits.txt#L932)).\r\n\r\nThe `register_visit()` is basically `add_path()` plus [extra manipulation with `count` and `latest`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/doc/mini-visits.txt#L470-L471). The result is not pruned during normalization.\r\n\r\nYou can see the currently active index and what effect `add_path` / `register_visit` have on it with `:=MiniVisits.get_index()`.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">add_path()</code> is a helper that <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/doc/mini-visits.txt#L482-L484\">ensures that path is present in the current index</a>. If it wasn't there, its <code class=\"notranslate\">count</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">latest</code> are 0, which means that entry will <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/doc/mini-visits.txt#L910-L915\">get pruned during normalization</a> before writing to the disk (because <code class=\"notranslate\">count</code> 0 is less than default <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/doc/mini-visits.txt#L932\">0.5 threshold</a>).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">register_visit()</code> is basically <code class=\"notranslate\">add_path()</code> plus <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/doc/mini-visits.txt#L470-L471\">extra manipulation with <code class=\"notranslate\">count</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">latest</code></a>. The result is not pruned during normalization.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">You can see the currently active index and what effect <code class=\"notranslate\">add_path</code> / <code class=\"notranslate\">register_visit</code> have on it with <code class=\"notranslate\">:=MiniVisits.get_index()</code>.</p>",
            "bodyText": "add_path() is a helper that ensures that path is present in the current index. If it wasn't there, its count and latest are 0, which means that entry will get pruned during normalization before writing to the disk (because count 0 is less than default 0.5 threshold).\nThe register_visit() is basically add_path() plus extra manipulation with count and latest. The result is not pruned during normalization.\nYou can see the currently active index and what effect add_path / register_visit have on it with :=MiniVisits.get_index().",
