                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "> So, how can I modify `count` and `latest` for `add_path`? Is it possible to do that? Could you please show me how to configure it?\r\n\r\nUse `register_visit` if you want to actually register a visit.\r\nIf you want to set some arbitrary values, then: [`get_index()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/doc/mini-visits.txt#L717), modify the table according to [its structure](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/doc/mini-visits.txt#L163), [`set_index()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/doc/mini-visits.txt#L725) or [`write_index()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/doc/mini-visits.txt#L771).",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">So, how can I modify <code class=\"notranslate\">count</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">latest</code> for <code class=\"notranslate\">add_path</code>? Is it possible to do that? Could you please show me how to configure it?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Use <code class=\"notranslate\">register_visit</code> if you want to actually register a visit.<br>\nIf you want to set some arbitrary values, then: <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/doc/mini-visits.txt#L717\"><code class=\"notranslate\">get_index()</code></a>, modify the table according to <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/doc/mini-visits.txt#L163\">its structure</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/doc/mini-visits.txt#L725\"><code class=\"notranslate\">set_index()</code></a> or <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/doc/mini-visits.txt#L771\"><code class=\"notranslate\">write_index()</code></a>.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "So, how can I modify count and latest for add_path? Is it possible to do that? Could you please show me how to configure it?\n\nUse register_visit if you want to actually register a visit.\nIf you want to set some arbitrary values, then: get_index(), modify the table according to its structure, set_index() or write_index().",
