                {
                    "author": {
                        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62192487?u=a36947d53d29eebdd44445978c89853446d108f0&v=4",
                        "login": "krovuxdev",
                        "resourcePath": "/krovuxdev",
                        "url": "https://github.com/krovuxdev"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "Thanks but when I tried `:=MiniVisits.write_index(\"/home/krovuxdev/.config/nvim\", {count = 1, latest = os.time() } )` I got an error:\r\n`E5108: Error executing lua (mini.visits) First level values in 'index' should be tables.`\r\n\r\n\r\nAlso, one more question: I [checked here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/doc/mini-visits.txt#L701-L715) is there any way to use a number in `iterate_paths(1)`? Something similar to Harpoon, like `harpoon:list():select(1)`, to be able to jump between multiple visits? Is it possible?",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks but when I tried <code class=\"notranslate\">:=MiniVisits.write_index(\"/home/krovuxdev/.config/nvim\", {count = 1, latest = os.time() } )</code> I got an error:<br>\n<code class=\"notranslate\">E5108: Error executing lua (mini.visits) First level values in 'index' should be tables.</code></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Also, one more question: I <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/doc/mini-visits.txt#L701-L715\">checked here</a> is there any way to use a number in <code class=\"notranslate\">iterate_paths(1)</code>? Something similar to Harpoon, like <code class=\"notranslate\">harpoon:list():select(1)</code>, to be able to jump between multiple visits? Is it possible?</p>",
                    "bodyText": "Thanks but when I tried :=MiniVisits.write_index(\"/home/krovuxdev/.config/nvim\", {count = 1, latest = os.time() } ) I got an error:\nE5108: Error executing lua (mini.visits) First level values in 'index' should be tables.\nAlso, one more question: I checked here is there any way to use a number in iterate_paths(1)? Something similar to Harpoon, like harpoon:list():select(1), to be able to jump between multiple visits? Is it possible?",
